  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combatting child labour in India through community empowerment, living income &amp; responsible mica supply chain practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to combat child labour through improved access to living income for mica dependent families and by protecting their human rights in mica supply chain of Jharkhand, India. The project will be implemented in parallel along the key nodes of upstream and the downstream length of mica supply chain between India and the Netherlands (30 mica dependent villages in Jharkhand, India). Through the community empowerment model, children and their mica dependent families will be empowered to access and influence authorities/duty bearers for social protection and positive alternatives to child labour. Through the cooperative model/upstream supply chain, mica dependent families will have improved access to living income with decent working conditions through a tested and replicable model for cooperatives of mic? workers and effective engagement of the upstream private sector for the implementation of the Dhibra policy guidelines.Finally, through the work on the downstream supply chain, with the partnership of the Dutch Cosmetics Association (NCV) and some of its members including L&apos;Or&#xe9;al and Rituals, companies in the Netherlands (and in the European Unioni (EU) by extension) will have increased knowledge, action perspective and guidance to undertake human rights due diligence, combat child labour and ensure a sustainable mica supply chain.</narrative>
  </description>
